{
  "title": "iOS UI tests: app main thread stalls for 30 s+ on CI outside the recipe screen",
  "description": "Two of the iOS UI flakes recorded here are fixed: (1) typed text not matching (server URL 'https://ramekin.ap…', a recipe saved as 'TextiOS text pancakes') came from the triple-tap clear in RecipeFlowTests selecting one word or nothing, and the tests now delete the old value character by character and check the result; (2) the hang after opening 'More recipe actions' (PR #729, run 37079044189) showed the app's main thread not servicing XCTest for about 3.5 minutes while the calorie estimate re-published an identical `resolving` response every 2 s, and UIKit logged menu updates during that time. \
The poll now publishes only a changed estimate. \
Still unexplained: (a) PR #722 run 36822014393 attempt 1: after Sign In in testRecipeFlow, the app's own log shows 'Unable to perform work on main run loop, process main thread busy for 30.0s' repeatedly (06:11–06:13), and snapshots still showed the login form. \
The likely suspect is the first recipe-cache sync: RecipeCacheStore is @MainActor, so applying each 100-recipe sync page (one fetch per recipe), reloading and JSON-decoding every cached recipe, and ranking search results all run on the main thread. \
Moving that work to a background context would rule it out. (b) PR #729 run 37082683506 attempt 2: testTextRecipeReviewAndSave stalled 36 s waiting for the app to idle on the login screen of a fresh launch, then failed with 'Failed to get list of active applications: Accessibility error kAXErrorIPCTimeout'. \
That looks like the simulator rather than the app. \
To diagnose: download the failed run's ios-ui-test-results artifact. \
The xcresult Data/ blobs are zstd-compressed; one holds the app's console log with the XCTPerformOnMainRunLoop busy messages and their timestamps.",
